       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum ibuprofen dose for adults. That maximum is 3,200 mg/day, usually given as 800 mg three or four times daily. A single 1600 mg dose is also well above the usual 800 mg maximum per dose. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot, and there's no added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common dose for inflammatory conditions\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day), typical for pain or fever\n\nOr did you mean 1600 mg total per day, for example 400 mg four times daily? Tell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give me a note for the order explaining why."
