       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. A confirmation alone doesn't change my concern. 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose and has no established clinical indication. The risk of serious harm is high, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. A normal baseline kidney and liver function doesn't offset that.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day), or whatever lower dose fits your goal.\n- **Help you escalate the question.** If you think there's an unusual reason for this dose, your attending or the inpatient pharmacist can review it. If they approve it, it can be entered through a pathway with that sign-off.\n- **Look at other options.** If pain control is inadequate on maximum-dose ibuprofen, adding scheduled acetaminophen or another analgesic is usually safer than going above the NSAID ceiling.\n\nTell me which dose you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
